<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analysis of Perceptual Modality.</span> To evaluate the contribution of each perceptual modality and the effectiveness of our unified videos introduced in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 MMPhysPipe ‣ 3 Method ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, we conduct a break-down ablation for the annotation pipeline in MMPhysPipe.
Specifically, we perform separate annotations for each perceptual modality on our constructed MMPhysData-36k dataset, including segmentation, pointmap (XYZ), and point tracking. Subsequently, we only replace our unified perceptual videos with single-modality counterparts for training. Based on the experimental results presented in Tab. <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Ablations and Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we draw the following observations: <span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1)</span> Our unified method outperforms all single-modality baselines, achieving the highest performance across average PC and SA scores. This indicates that our unified videos provide rich, complementary physical content for VDMs. <span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2)</span> Among the single-modality variants, instance segmentation provides the most substantial improvement in the model’s semantic alignment.
Furthermore, we demonstrate the visual results of our dual-stream teacher models, which simultaneously generate RGB videos and corresponding perceptual predictions. As shown in Fig. <a href="#S4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 4.2 Main results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the pointmap modality enables MMPhysVideo to disentangle foreground subjects from complex background in open scenes, while the integration of segmentation and point tracking enables a granular focus on physical dynamics, spanning from rigid-body motion to fluid ripples.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02817v1/distillation_radar.png" id="S4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:537/166;" width="537" height="166" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span><span id="S4.F8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation study</span> of our distillation utilizing representation alignment based on CogVideoX-2B, CogVideoX-5B and Wan2.1-1.3B from left to right, respectively.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Component Effectiveness of MMPhysPipe.</span> In Tab. <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.3 Ablations and Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we analyze the importance of each component in MMPhysPipe through a break-down ablation. The baseline is directly finetuning CogVideoX-2B on a randomly selected subset of OpenVidHD-0.4M, without joint multimodal modeling. We incrementally incorporate the components while maintaining a constant number of finetuning data. In general, our proposed components in MMPhysPipe consistently enhance model performance across both Average PC and SA scores. Especially, the Average PC score achieves a substantial improvement of <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.5\%</annotation></semantics></math> compared to the baseline. Together, our proposed components complement each other to effectively curate high-quality and diverse real-world data with rich physical phenomena.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effectiveness of Distillation.</span> In Fig. <a href="#S4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 4.3 Ablations and Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we evaluate the impact of our relation-based distillation on single-stream student models across various backbones. Concretely, we compare the distilled student model against the dual-stream teacher model, a teacher model variant outputting RGB without perceptual control signals, and the baseline. Generally, the performance of the student model is on par with that of the dual-stream teacher model and consistently outperforms the teacher model variant, underscoring the necessity of our distillation process.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we propose MMPhysVideo, a novel framework designed to enhance the physical consistency of video generation through joint multimodal modeling. To achieve this, we first develop an innovative dual-stream teacher architecture to decouple the processing of RGB and perceptual modalities, distilling it into a single-stream student via representation alignment. Complementing this, we propose MMPhysPipe, an end-to-end pipeline for curating data with rich physical interactions and generating multi-granular perceptual annotations. Both quantitative and qualitative results on the physics-focused benchmarks demonstrate the superiority of MMPhysVideo with consistent gains across advanced models, setting a new state-of-the-art for physics-consistent video generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
