</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Statistical Overview</h3>

<div id="A2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our MMPhysPipe is designed as a modular and scalable engine. The transition from 433k raw samples to 36k curated samples represents a strategic shift from ’quantity’ to ’quality-plus-modality,’ where each retained sample is enriched with synchronized geometric and temporal trajectories that are absent in vanilla video datasets. Due to its automated nature, this pipeline can be deployed to any text-video datasets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="A2.T6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results on Videophy</span> using the VideoCon-Physics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bansal et al. (2024)</a></cite> evaluator. <sup id="A2.T6.5" class="ltx_sup">†</sup> denotes results from WISA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025c)</a></cite>. * denotes results from VideoREPA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025b)</a></cite>.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T6.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
