</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>More Quantitative Results</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Results on Videophy</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our model using the VideoCon-Physics evaluator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bansal et al., 2024</a>)</cite> on Videophy to compare with more physics methods and base models. The results in Tab. <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ B.6 Statistical Overview ‣ Appendix B More Details of MMPhysPipe ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> lead to two key observations: <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span> MMPhysVideo consistently enhances the physical plausibility of various base models. Notably, when applied to CogVideoX-5B, our method achieves a state-of-the-art Average PC of 41.0 and Average SA of 72.7. <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span> MMPhysVideo demonstrates significant gains across all interaction types. For instance, on the Wan2.1-1.3B base, our method improves the PC for Solid-Fluid interactions from 25.3 to 29.5 and Fluid-Fluid from 41.8 to 47.3.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluator Comparison.</span> while our results demonstrate consistent improvement across both evaluators on both physics benchmarks (VideoPhy, PhyGenBench), we further compare VideoCon-Physics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bansal et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and Videoscore2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. As shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ B.6 Statistical Overview ‣ Appendix B More Details of MMPhysPipe ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, Videoscore2 delivers fine-grained diagnostics by generating interpretable reasoning that identifies specific failure modes (e.g., causal inconsistencies or unnatural motion). This capability yields more robust and accurate evaluations, going beyond scalar scores to explain <span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">why</span> a video is physically implausible.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T7" class="ltx_table">
