<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Results on VBench</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further evaluate the impact of MMPhysVideo on general video generation quality, we conduct the evaluation using the VBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> suite. The results in Tab. <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ C.1 Results on Videophy ‣ Appendix C More Quantitative Results ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> lead to following key observations: <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1)</span> MMPhysVideo consistently outperforms the base models across the majority of quality dimensions, demonstrating that our joint multimodal modeling with representation distillation does not compromise, but rather enhances, the overall generative performance. <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2)</span> MMPhysVideo significantly improves spatio-temporal metrics (e.g., Subject Consistency, Motion Smoothness), indicating that internalizing geometric and trajectory cues strengthens scene structural constraints and object persistence. (3) MMPhysVideo also boosts aesthetic and imaging quality. Notably, it increases the Imaging Quality of Wan2.1-1.3B from 67.0 to 68.3.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>More Qualitative Results</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present additional qualitative comparisons under various backbone configurations, including CogVideoX-2B (Fig. <a href="#A4.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ Appendix D More Qualitative Results ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), CogVideoX-5B (Fig. <a href="#A4.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ Appendix D More Qualitative Results ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), and Wan2.1-1.3B (Fig. <a href="#A4.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ Appendix D More Qualitative Results ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). Further visualizations of joint RGB-perception generation are provided in Fig. <a href="#A4.F18" title="Figure 18 ‣ Appendix D More Qualitative Results ‣ MMPhysVideo: Scaling Physical Plausibility in Video Generation via Joint Multimodal Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>. We encourage readers to view the accompanying MP4 videos along with our appendix.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02817v1/CogvideoX-2B_Comparison_Case.png" id="A4.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:521/792;" width="521" height="792" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span><span id="A4.F15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">More qualitative comparison</span> with CogVideoX-2B backbones.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02817v1/CogvideoX-5B_Comparison_Case.png" id="A4.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:521/788;" width="521" height="788" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 16: </span><span id="A4.F16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">More qualitative comparison</span> with CogVideoX-5B backbones.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F17" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02817v1/Wan2p1_1p3_Comparison_Case.png" id="A4.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:499/564;" width="499" height="564" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 17: </span><span id="A4.F17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">More qualitative comparison</span> with Wan2.1-1.3B backbones.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F18" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2604.02817v1/perception_Case.png" id="A4.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:494/220;" width="494" height="220" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 18: </span><span id="A4.F18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">More visualization</span> of joint generation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
